WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.141
Week 10: Likes, Preferences, and Leisure. express likes and dislikes invite and suggest compare activities

2
00:00:07.141 --> 00:00:13.492
Cultural lens. Football, music, outdoor recreation, and local leisure practices.

3
00:00:13.492 --> 00:00:25.350
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:25.350 --> 00:00:36.973
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:36.973 --> 00:00:45.802
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:45.802 --> 00:01:13.020
Model language. Me gusta escuchar música en vivo. — I like listening to live music. A Tomás le interesan los documentales. — Tomás is interested in documentaries. ¿Prefieres salir o quedarte en casa? — Do you prefer going out or staying home? Nos encanta jugar juntos. — We love playing together. El senderismo es más tranquilo que el fútbol. — Hiking is calmer than soccer.

7
00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:22.769
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
